# Formal Justice

*Formal Justices, justice as regularity, justice as regularities, Formal Justices, justice as regularities, Formal Justices, justice as regularities*

The equal and impartial application of laws/rules in all cases.

---

# Primary Goods

(Rawls) Rights and liberties, power and opportunities, and income and wealth.

---

# General Conception of Justice

*General Conception of Justices, General Conception of Justices, General Conception of Justices*

(Rawls) All social primary goods are to be distributed equally unless an unequal distribution of any of these goods is to the advantage of the least favored. In other words, it is the difference principle applied to all primary social goods.
By following in accordance to the general conception, we can eventually eliminate natural and limitations and historical injustices and ensure that less than equal liberty would no longer by acceptable.

---

# Desert-based Meritocracy

*Desert-based Meritocracies, deontological meritocracy, deontological meritocracies, desert-based merit, desert-based merits, Desert-based Meritocracies, deontological meritocracies, desert-based merits, Desert-based Meritocracies, deontological meritocracies, desert-based merits*

Allocation of social goods is intrinsically justified because individuals deserve outcomes proportional to their merits.

